[7.123,"o","\r\n🔍 Routing exclusions — 7 active:\r\n\r\n  🔒 bedrock — skipped by the model registry (every tracked model is unavailable or quota-parked). Run `nuvira models unblock bedrock` once it recovers.\r\n  🚫 gemini/gpt-oss:120b-cloud — this model does not exist on that provider (it answered \"not found\"). It will not be offered again unless a probe proves it works.\r\n  🚫 groq/groq/compound-mini — this model does not exist on that provider (it answered \"not found\"). It will not be offered again unless a probe proves it works.\r\n  🚫 groq/groq/compound — this model does not exist on that provider (it answered \"not found\"). It will not be offered again unless a probe proves it works.\r\n  🚫 groq/gemini-3.1-flash-lite — this model does not exist on that provider (it answered \"not found\"). It will not be offered again unless a probe proves it works.\r\n  🚫 groq/gpt-oss:120b-cloud — this model does not exist on that provider (it answered \"not found\"). It will not be offered again unless a probe proves it works.\r\n  🚫 groq/gemma-4-26b-a4b-it — this model does not exist on that provider (it answered \"not found\"). It will not be offered again unless a probe proves it works.\r\n\r\n♻️  Recovered (no longer skipped):\r\n\r\n  ✅ gemini/gemini-3.6-flash — unknown failure from 2026-09-25 08:05 UTC has expired; routable now.\r\n\r\n👀 A provider that stays skipped with a working key is a bug — `nuvira models unblock <provider>` forces a re-probe.\r\nℹ️  Not listed here (SELECTION-only, never a hard block): the admin max-cost cap and minSpeed/minReasoning.\r\n   They reorder candidates on the auto path only; an explicit --provider pin is respected as your choice.\r\n"]
